    {"d":9.67,"cues":[0.8],"say":["Day 47. Validating forms with the browser, collecting their data, and handling files and uploads."]},
    {"d":31.518,"cues":[0.3,9.008,16.228,23.761],"say":["Start with H T M L. Attributes like required, type email, min, and pattern describe what valid input looks like.","On submit, the browser checks every field before the submit event fires, and stops at the first problem.","Each input has a validity object, with one flag per rule it breaks, and valid, when it passes them all.","Pick the right type, input mode, and autocomplete too. The right keyboard and autofill come for free."]},
    {"d":30.522,"cues":[0.3,8.612,17.369,23.522],"say":["Check validity returns true or false. Report validity does the same check, and also shows the message to the user.","Set custom validity adds your own error, like, code already used, from the server. Now the field is invalid.","It stays invalid, even after the user edits it, until you clear it with an empty string.","Add no validate to the form to draw your own error U I, while still using the same validity checks."]},
    {"d":30.409,"cues":[0.3,6.647,12.931,21.419],"say":["On submit, new form data of the form collects the value of every named, enabled field.","Unchecked checkboxes, disabled fields, and inputs without a name, are skipped entirely.","Repeated names give several entries. Get all keeps them all. Object dot from entries keeps only the last one.","Listen for submit, not a button click, so the enter key and request submit work too. Then call prevent default."]},
    {"d":27.421,"cues":[0.3,7.562,13.972,19.305],"say":["Every field needs a real label. Link its error text with aria described by, and set aria invalid.","Announce errors with role alert, or a live region, and move focus to the first invalid field.","Never rely on colour, or a placeholder alone, to say what is wrong.","And client checks are only a convenience. Anyone can skip them, so the server validates everything again."]},
    {"d":32.666,"cues":[0.3,8.333,16.671,24.876],"say":["An input of type file gives you a file list of file objects, each with a name, size, type, and last modified.","File extends blob, so you read it with text, array buffer, or stream. Prefer those to the older file reader.","For a preview, U R L dot create object U R L gives a blob U R L. Revoke it when you are done, or the memory leaks.","But file dot type comes from the file name. It can lie, so the server must check the real bytes."]},
    {"d":31.934,"cues":[0.3,5.6,13.557,23.23],"say":["To upload, append the file to a form data, and post it with fetch.","Do not set the content type header yourself. The browser adds it, with the multipart boundary the server needs.","Fetch has no upload progress. X M L H T T P request does. Upload dot on progress drives a progress bar.","Give users a cancel button. Abort with an abort controller for fetch, or x h r dot abort for X H R."]},
    {"d":30.441,"cues":[0.3,8.943,16.355,21.441],"say":["A big file over a shaky network often fails as one long request. So cut it into chunks, with file dot slice.","Send each chunk with its offset and a checksum, so the server can verify it, and put the file back together.","If the connection drops, ask the server for the last offset it confirmed.","Then resend only the rest. The tus protocol, and S 3 multipart uploads, work exactly like this."]},
    {"d":34.16,"cues":[0.3,8.758,17,26.218],"say":["For a drop zone, call prevent default in drag enter and drag over. Otherwise, the drop event never fires.","In the drop handler, read event dot data transfer dot files. Keep a real file input for keyboard users.","Navigator dot clipboard dot write text copies text. It needs a secure context, and a user gesture, like a click.","Reading the clipboard may ask for permission. The paste event gives you clipboard data, without a prompt."]},
    {"d":14,"cues":[0.5],"say":["Recap. Now open the Day 47 topics below, and run every example yourself."]}
